    "title": "Around the Block: Cyclosporiasis in Oklahoma - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Jacquelyn Farris/KFOR ,\n6 hours ago OKLAHOMA CITY (KFOR) – Happy Wednesday Oklahoma!. Here are a few topics we went over on today’s show. An outbreak of a parasite, known to cause “explosive diarrhea” is growing. Dozens of cases have just been confirmed here in Oklahoma. The State Health Department sent out an alert to doctors today about Cyclosporiasis. So far, there are 56 known cases in the state. Six people were so sick they had to be hospitalized. The CDC has yet to pinpoint the cause of the outbreak. Read full article\n2",
